## at the zone's edge. The test takes the attributes each shader gets from the meshes at the same points of the board's
## faces, evaluates a GDScript mirror of the shaders' colour (the branch chosen by the same flags as the shaders) on a grid
## across the seam and fails when the two colours differ by more than TOL in any channel. Also: every operand of the
## CSG zone carries the board's wood flag (UV.y 2, UV.x = half diagonal). Prints BOARD_SEAM_DONE ok=... fails=...

const TOL := 0.02
var fails := 0


func _ready() -> void:
